  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Identifying associative entrepreneurship groups led by women to achieve their economic autonomy.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute to the improvement of living conditions and quality of life for women in the poorest and most excluded communities of El Salvador by strengthening their ability to earn a living. 

The project will achieve this through managing a business environment based on a solidary economy, including increased self-esteem, equality, and economic empowerment. The communities will also learn to better manage the environment, including natural resources and farming practices, and increasing resilience to the negative impacts and shocks of climate change and changing weather patterns. 

The specific objective of the project is to improve the socio-economic conditions of these women by strengthening their access to credit and creating a savings initiative (caja rural) to be used as seed capital to buy land and other assets for family production.</narrative>
  </description>
